Exp :Fibonacci Series

Aim:
To write a Java program to print the Fibonacci series up to n terms.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Scanner package.
3. Read the number of terms from the user.
4. Initialize a = 0 and b = 1.
5. Print the first two numbers of the series as applicable.
6. Calculate the next term using c = a + b.
7. Update a = b and b = c.
8. Repeat until n terms are printed.
9. Stop the program.

Program:

import java.util.Scanner;
public class FibonacciSeries {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n, a = 0, b = 1, c;

        System.out.print("Enter number of terms: ");
        n = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.println("Fibonacci Series:");

        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            System.out.print(a + " ");
            c = a + b;
            a = b;
            b = c;
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}

